WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:06.880
So the Game of Thrones show is based off a
really long series of books.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.620
Longer than The Lord of the Rings and the
Bible combined – and the series hasn’t

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.400
even all been written yet.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:20.130
So to fit this huge story into seventy-three
hours of TV, the show cuts out a lot of characters

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:25.710
and plots from the books, which kinda sucks,
cause a lot of them are really cool and mysterious

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.950
– for example, the story of Gerion Lannister.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.749
The Lannisters we meet in the show include
Tywin – father of Cersei, Jaime and Tyrion

00:00:34.749 --> 00:00:39.430
– and Tywin’s brother Kevan – father
of Lancel, Martyn and Willem.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.960
But in the books, Tywin has three more siblings
– there’s Genna Lannister, a smart, domineering

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.120
woman married to a Frey, and Tygett Lannister,
a skilled warrior who died of a pox years

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.590
ago, and then there’s Gerion.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.630
Gerion was Tyrion and Jaime’s favourite
uncle growing up . He taught Tyrion to tumble,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:02.239
to cartwheel and walk on his hands , and encouraged
him to learn about the wonders of the world

00:01:02.239 --> 00:01:08.540
. This was in contrast to the eldest Lannister
Tywin, always so stern and serious . Tygett

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.700
and Gerion felt they were in Tywin’s shadow,
but while Tyg got angry that he could never

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.330
match Tywin, Gerion would make a joke of it
all – “Better to mock the game than to

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.330
play and lose” . So Gerion travelled the
east , he competed in tournaments , he fathered

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:27.110
a bastard daughter, Joy, by a common woman,
Briony . And then about seven years before

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:32.510
the start of the main story, Gerion went on
a quest to find House Lannister’s lost Valyrian

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:38.000
steel sword, Brightroar .
So Valyrian steel is a magical metal , made

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.180
in Valyria centuries ago.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.240
It was used to make weapons, like swords,
that were sharper, stronger and lighter than

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.049
swords of regular steel . But when Valyria
blew up, in the Doom, the secret of making

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:54.140
the steel was lost . Now, there are only a
couple of hundred Valyrian steel blades left

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:59.229
in Westeros . Many of them are treasured as
the heirlooms of noble houses – for example,

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:04.119
Heartsbane is the Valyrian blade of House
Tarly, and Longclaw was the sword of House

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:09.490
Mormont until Jeor gave it to Jon Snow – in
the show, Jon discovers Valyrian steel can

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:14.330
kill white walkers , which is another reason
it’s important.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:18.820
Brightroar was once the Valyrian blade of
House Lannister – they paid a huge amount

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:24.670
of gold for in the years before the Doom . But
about a century later, after Valyria was destroyed,

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:29.090
King Tommen Lannister went on an expedition
to plunder the ruins of Valyria.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:34.470
He took Brightroar with him – and “never
returned” . So Brightroar, one of House

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.450
Lannister’s most valuable treasures, was
lost, and ever since, they’ve tried to replace

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.450
it.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.870
Tywin offered to buy Valyrian swords from
poorer houses, but was always refused . So

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.930
Gerion, the more adventurous, or perhaps just
“reckless” Lannister , decided to go find

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:57.060
Brightroar himself, where Tommen lost it centuries
ago – in the ruins of Valyria .

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:02.480
Valyria was once the capital of a prosperous,
powerful empire, but after its mysterious

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.830
destruction, a smoking broken ruin remains.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.800
In the show, Tyrion and Jorah sail through
it like it ain’t no thang, but in the books,

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.060
Valyria’s cursed.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:16.710
It’s said the very sea there boils and smokes,
the land is overrun with demons, and anyone

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:22.010
who “lays eyes upon [its] coast is doomed”
. Whole armies have marched into Valyria and

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.300
never returned . But that didn’t stop Gerion.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:30.440
He set sail from Lannisport, and headed for
Valyria . When he stopped off at Volantis,

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:34.200
half his crew deserted him, and he had to
buy slaves to replace them, cause everyone

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:40.209
was so scared of sailing the Smoking Sea . After
Volantis, Gerion disappeared – and was never

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:41.270
seen again.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:43.319
So… what happened?

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:44.760
There are lots of different theories.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.360
The most obvious one is that Gerion died in
Valyria.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.220
We don’t know exactly what the dangers of
Valyria are, whether they’re toxic volcanic

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.940
fumes, or demons, or magic, but there’s
clearly something nasty there, cause it’s

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:01.330
killed so many people before – Gerion’s
ancestor Tommen included.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:06.790
Gerion might also have been shipwrecked, attacked
by pirates, or killed in a mutiny of his crew.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.330
However it happened, it’s a likely explanation
– that Gerion is dead and won’t be seen

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.680
again.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.519
But there are other theories.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:19.130
Not everyone who’s sailed to Valyria has
died – Euron Greyjoy claims to have been

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.330
there , and it looks like he’s telling the
truth, cause in the books he has a Valyrian

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:28.270
dragon horn , and a set of Valyrian steel
armour . If Euron has been to Valyria, and

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:33.069
Gerion apparently died there, maybe Euron
and Gerion ran into each other, maybe Euron

00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:38.639
killed or captured Gerion, maybe Gerion is
one of the mute oarsmen on Euron’s ship

00:04:38.639 --> 00:04:44.229
the Silence – but… this is unlikely because
of the timelines – Gerion sailed for Valyria

00:04:44.229 --> 00:04:48.999
about eight years ago , but Euron went on
his big voyage about two years ago – so

00:04:48.999 --> 00:04:54.370
unless Gerion was hanging around in Valyria
for six years, he wouldn’t have met Euron

00:04:54.370 --> 00:05:00.199
there . Another theory is that Gerion became
the “corsair king”, a pirate who’s been

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:04.770
mentioned raiding round the Summer Isles,
but again, the timeline doesn’t fit.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:10.520
The corsair king is “new” , only recently
started raiding, so if the corsair is Gerion,

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.409
what was he doing these last eight years?

00:05:13.409 --> 00:05:18.610
One of the crazier theories is that Gerion
is the Shrouded Lord, a mysterious mystical

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:23.189
figure who lives in the Sorrows, which Tyrion
passes through in Dance.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:27.759
YouTuber Preston Jacobs argues that the Lord
seems to spare Tyrion from getting greyscale

00:05:27.759 --> 00:05:32.299
from stone men , that both Gerion and the
Shrouded Lord are associated with laughter

00:05:32.299 --> 00:05:37.229
, and that the Lord must look like Gerion
because Tyrion dreams of the Lord being Tywin

00:05:37.229 --> 00:05:41.370
. It’s a fun idea, but the text doesn’t
really support it.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:46.270
The dream has nothing to with Gerion, the
laughter connection is barely mentioned in

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:50.020
the text, and the Lord sparing Tyrion is tenuous
at best.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:55.270
To complicate things some more, it is mentioned
that this “corsair king” supposedly is

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:00.699
the current Shrouded Lord – shit’s most
assuredly confusing and complex, but in the

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:05.789
end, there’s just no good evidence that
Gerion is the Shrouded Lord or the corsair

00:06:05.789 --> 00:06:08.429
king, or anybody else.

00:06:08.429 --> 00:06:13.639
Not every missing character has a twist and
a secret identity – Gerion probably is just

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:18.179
dead in Valyria – but there’s still another
theory to address.

00:06:18.179 --> 00:06:23.830
It’s about a woman called the Sailor’s
Wife, a prostitute in Braavos who only beds

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:29.080
the men who marry her in fun little temporary
wedding ceremonies . The Sailor’s Wife has

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.979
a daughter, called Lanna , who has “fine
long golden hair” . Blonde hair and the

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:37.539
name Lanna make the girl sound like a Lannister
, right?

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:41.669
And we hear that the Sailor’s Wife prays
for “her first husband, her true husband”,

00:06:41.669 --> 00:06:47.250
“her old love”, “who had been lost at
sea” . Maybe the Sailor’s Wife’s “first

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:51.699
husband”, and the father of her blonde daughter
Lanna, is Gerion Lannister.

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:56.679
Gerion was “lost at sea”, that’s the
exact phrase consistently used to describe

00:06:56.679 --> 00:07:00.620
him . And Gerion would explain Lanna’s blonde
hair and name.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.409
Further, the fortune-teller Yna , claims that
the Sailor’s Wife’s husband is dead – which

00:07:05.409 --> 00:07:09.479
fits the idea that Gerion died in Valyria.

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:14.209
So this seems like pretty strong theory but
again – the timing’s tricky.

00:07:14.209 --> 00:07:19.309
Lanna is fourteen in the fourth book , which
means she was fathered years before Gerion

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:24.180
sailed to find Brightroar, which is fine,
cause we know he travelled the east before,

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.889
but remember Gerion’s daughter Joy?

00:07:26.889 --> 00:07:32.959
She is eleven in the fourth book . Which means
for Gerion to have fathered both Joy and Lanna,

00:07:32.959 --> 00:07:37.369
he must have sailed to Braavos, married the
Sailor’s Wife and fathered Lanna, then left

00:07:37.369 --> 00:07:43.069
and just two years later fathered Joy on Briony
in Westeros – and a few years after that

00:07:43.069 --> 00:07:45.379
sailed to Valyria and died.

00:07:45.379 --> 00:07:48.489
Which is… possible, but seems weird.

00:07:48.489 --> 00:07:54.080
It totally undercuts the whole tragic love
story of the Sailor’s Wife if her long lost

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:58.479
husband actually just dumped her and left
to hook up with someone else.

00:07:58.479 --> 00:08:03.370
Also, the Sailor’s Wife was “no older”
than fourteen when her husband left, and she

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.400
and her child both work as prostitutes to
support themselves.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.749
Why would Gerion not send a little Lannister
gold their way at some point?

00:08:11.749 --> 00:08:16.020
Joy seems to be pretty well supported – why
treat the Sailor’s Wife differently?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:21.430
Tyrion’s favourite uncle doesn’t sound
like the sorta guy to so coldly abandon a

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.759
loving wife and child.

00:08:23.759 --> 00:08:24.869
So what gives?

00:08:24.869 --> 00:08:29.279
The might be a solution in the timing.

00:08:29.279 --> 00:08:33.650
While writing the fourth Game of Thrones book,
George Martin planned to leave a “five-year

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:38.590
gap” between the third and fourth books,
meaning Book 4 would pick up the story five

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:43.620
years after the third, with all the characters
five years older – Arya would have spent

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:47.910
five years training with the Faceless Men,
Bran would have been learning from Bloodraven

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:52.870
– but Martin found the gap didn’t work
so well for other characters, so after a year

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:58.839
of writing with the gap, he scrapped it, and
instead had Book 4 pick up where Book 3 ended

00:08:58.839 --> 00:09:02.940
. This meant he had to go back and re-write
a lot of what he’d already written, changing

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.930
stuff to remove the gap.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:09.620
He would have had to change details like dates
and years and… ages.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:14.870
The five-year gap made everyone five years
older, so to remove the gap from what he’d

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:20.569
already written he’d have to make some characters
five years younger and maybe – just maybe

00:09:20.569 --> 00:09:25.830
– he made a mistake – and forgot to change
back the age of Lanna.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:30.770
Because if Lanna was five years younger, she’d
be nine instead of fourteen, which would mean

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:35.470
she could have been conceived the same year
that Gerion sailed for Valyria.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.370
Which changes everything.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:41.310
Instead of Gerion having to sail to Braavos,
marry then dump the Wife, go back to Westeros,

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.569
father Joy, then sail to Valyria, he could
have just stopped off in Braavos and met the

00:09:45.569 --> 00:09:50.910
Wife along the way to Valyria – with every
intention of coming back to her – until

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:55.610
he was tragically “lost at sea”, leaving
the Wife and Lanna longing, never knowing

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.639
if he’d return.

00:09:57.639 --> 00:10:03.560
That fits the tragic story of the Sailor’s
Wife much better, and the math works perfectly

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:08.269
– Lanna’s fourteen in Feast, minus five
for the gap makes nine, so she’d be born

00:10:08.269 --> 00:10:10.319
in the year 291.

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:17.240
Gerion sailed eight years before Storm, which
happens in 299, so he sailed in about 291.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:24.630
It looks very very possible that George Martin
made a small mistake with Lanna’s age.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:27.670
So Gerion probably didn’t meet Euron.

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.970
He probably isn’t a corsair, or the Shrouded
Lord.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:36.579
He’s probably a corpse somewhere in Valyria
– which is all the more tragic cause it

00:10:36.579 --> 00:10:41.480
looks like he left behind a child and a Wife
who love him, who he may have meant to return

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.850
to until he sadly died.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:50.730
And you almost wouldn’t know it cause it
may be George forgot to do some math.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.000
Thanks for watching.

